                        ],
                        "form": "die Christenheit"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fbe91171-9c91-3483-80db-319098b75aa3",
                        "entry_id": "2cecdc68-1c6f-33f9-9d64-6e23833e67bc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Gesamtheit aller Christen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b178870a-ef5d-485d-8c6a-fb3d28e8780f",
                                "sense_id": "fbe91171-9c91-3483-80db-319098b75aa3",
                                "text": "„Auf dem Gelände der kaiserlichen Gardetruppen, deren Kaserne er abzureißen befahl, ließ Konstantin die Lateranbasilika errichten, die sich im Laufe der Jahrhunderte als Mittelpunkt der westlichen Christenheit behaupten sollte.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9b657b4-d715-4e0f-8b2f-7b85471ce553",
                                "sense_id": "fbe91171-9c91-3483-80db-319098b75aa3",
                                "text": "„Viele Männer waren zuvor schon auf den Scheiterhaufen der Christenheit ein Opfer der Flammen geworden.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "25afac09-1cbf-48e8-9d60-2dbf489a9cfc",
                                "sense_id": "fbe91171-9c91-3483-80db-319098b75aa3",
                                "text": "„Das Rom der Päpste, Sehnsucht und Ziel unzähliger Pilger, war unter den großen Päpsten des Hochmittelalters nicht mehr nur religiöser Mittelpunkt der abendländischen Christenheit, sondern auch geistlich-weltliche Metropole.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8a2def58-fe62-46e3-9fb3-30b101392eb6",
                        "source_entry_id": "2cecdc68-1c6f-33f9-9d64-6e23833e67bc",
                        "source_sense_id": "fbe91171-9c91-3483-80db-319098b75aa3",
                        "source_sense_description": "Gesamtheit aller Christen",
                        "target_lang_word": "Christendom",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Christendom",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e97dd23a-fe76-36da-bec8-d4caf7ecab90",
                                        "entry_id": "d956ca24-64d9-35cc-8670-38045f3eca15",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The Christian world; Christ's Church on Earth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abc874ab-635c-4227-b85f-3e0691d13f9b",
                                                "sense_id": "e97dd23a-fe76-36da-bec8-d4caf7ecab90",
                                                "text": "The Arian doctrine which then divided Christendom."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efd3e1db-bf24-4bd3-a9be-2455b87a9759",
                                                "sense_id": "e97dd23a-fe76-36da-bec8-d4caf7ecab90",
                                                "text": "The result is contained in the fact of a wide and still widening Christendom."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc0a3956-f991-4bff-af21-fe4a03f1ad88",
                                                "sense_id": "e97dd23a-fe76-36da-bec8-d4caf7ecab90",
                                                "text": "Wessex was facing new barbarians, apparently intent on destroying everything that Christendom meant for England."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99119bad-92d6-3bd6-b08e-98b3698b076b",
                                        "entry_id": "d956ca24-64d9-35cc-8670-38045f3eca15",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being a (devout) Christian; Christian belief or faith."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63723cfc-e057-4bbc-9e50-72d36a7b2379",
                                                "sense_id": "99119bad-92d6-3bd6-b08e-98b3698b076b",
                                                "text": "By my Chriſtendome, So I were out of priſon, and kept Sheepe, I ſhould be as merry as the day is long."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61ce5cab-d218-403a-9385-1ef51bfae375",
                                                "sense_id": "99119bad-92d6-3bd6-b08e-98b3698b076b",
                                                "text": "[…]and yet cannot be denied that ſo it ought to be, by any man that would not have his Chriſtendome ſuſpected."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5c46026-7b82-4cd0-a31f-574f89dbe2c2",
                                                "sense_id": "99119bad-92d6-3bd6-b08e-98b3698b076b",
                                                "text": "Especially about law and its obligatory force was Cromwell's head clear, making clearer distinctions than Wolsey with his conscience or More with his Christendom."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a110dfc-23c4-3cfc-91de-9480f797f50e",
                                        "entry_id": "d956ca24-64d9-35cc-8670-38045f3eca15",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The name received at baptism; any name or appellation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9cadae5a-6e1b-4241-83ab-a76c6802805b",
                                                "sense_id": "3a110dfc-23c4-3cfc-91de-9480f797f50e",
                                                "text": "[…]but for an Author to renounce his Chriſtendome to write in his owne commendation, to refuſe the name which his Godfathers and Godmothers gaue him in his baptiſme , and call himſelfe a wellwiller to both the writers[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fbd0a4d-8db8-4214-9779-b6c378cc2bc3",
                                                "sense_id": "3a110dfc-23c4-3cfc-91de-9480f797f50e",
                                                "text": "His faith, his ſweet diſaſter: with a world\n Of pretty fond adoptious chriſtendomes\n That blinking Cupid goſſips."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
